  "_version": "1.0.0",
  "_description": "Workday System Audit Log → AKSI control ID mapping. Workday is the dominant enterprise HR + finance system and the canonical evidence source for who-touched-which-employee-record. Agents reading worker, compensation, performance, or PII data trigger massive regulated-PII exposure (HIPAA-adjacent benefits data, SOX-relevant compensation, GDPR/PIPEDA cross-jurisdiction worker records). Each event_type carries a different risk profile: Login is identity (PR-01), View_Compensation/View_Salary/View_PII are exfiltration surface (PR-04), Edit_Compensation/Configure_Security/Bulk_Edit are scope-changing (PR-02), Add_Worker/Terminate_Worker are audit-trail (PR-05). Service-account access to compensation data is the highest-risk pattern (FAIL → BLOCK). Cross-worker access by a single actor (>30 distinct workers/hr) and out-of-region access (>10 records crossing GDPR/PIPEDA jurisdiction) produce synthetic PR-04 findings. Identifiers are heavily sanitized: worker_id and target_worker_id reduced to last-8, full names stored as length only, cost_center to last-8, client_ip to /16, integration_system_id to last-8 — Workday IDs encode tenant/org structure.",
